      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alamo%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Alamo was laid out and platted in 1837, marking its formal establishment.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alamo%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1859 a road linked Alamo to Crawfordsville, and the Yountsville Covered Bridge was built.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alamo%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The post office at Alamo has been in operation since 1844, serving the community for over a century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alamo%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Alamo sits 13 miles southwest of Crawfordsville, the county seat of Montgomery County.",
